     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Followup from Sourceforge Tracker&#93;</span><br/>\nFollowup Submitter: sjw46<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=1709161<br/>\nOriginator: YES</p>\n\n<p>When running an itql query like so:</p>\n\n<p>select $tpackage $relDate<br/>\nfrom &lt;#ri&gt;<br/>\nwhere $tpackage<br/>\n&lt;<a href=\"http://localhost:8880/NCCS/ontologies/relationships#isDistributedBy\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8880/NCCS/ontologies/relationships#isDistributedBy</a>&gt;<br/>\n&lt;info:fedora/test:target1&gt;<br/>\nand $tpackage<br/>\n&lt;<a href=\"http://localhost:8880/NCCS/ontologies/relationships#hasReleaseDate\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8880/NCCS/ontologies/relationships#hasReleaseDate</a>&gt; $relDate<br/>\nand $relDate &lt;<a href=\"http://tucana.org/tucana#gt\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://tucana.org/tucana#gt</a>&gt; '12' in &lt;#xsd&gt;</p>\n\n<p>... it only works if the datatype of #hasReleaseDate is defined as xsd:double<br/>\n(not int) in RELS-EXT.  This may be a bug in the version of Kowari we're<br/>\ncurrently using (1.0.5).  In the mean time, if people need to do numeric<br/>\ncomparisons, they can use xsd:double rather than int.</p>",
     "created": "12/Mar/07 5:25 PM",
